      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T23:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you identify the implications of adding/removing uris and then reloading the plugin? Will we be left over with tasks in storage that wont ever get picked up?",
      "revId": "519e19ac380c68a097d237bf5d35454692ba71e6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7db87978_5d1a7630",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/googlesource/gerrit/plugins/replication/UrlDistributionStrategy.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 4651293
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-20T16:28:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Tasks are persisted per URI by every strategy, so a pending task for a URI that was removed matches no destination on reload and stays in storage; that is pre-existing and not specific to refSharded. For URIs that remain, a pending task is still pushed to its stored URI even if the ref\u0027s owner moved, which costs at most one duplicate write, never a loss. Added a doc note to run a full sync after changing the URL list.",
      "parentUuid": "7292ae91_98234782",
      "revId": "519e19ac380c68a097d237bf5d35454692ba71e6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
